            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0005-Adding-Mctp-Over-Spi-Driver.patch",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The DMTF hasn't standardized an \"MCTP over SPI\" binding though, have they?  When this is upstream it should probably be very clear that this is an nvidia-specific protocol."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0005-Adding-Mctp-Over-Spi-Driver.patch",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ACK, can make that more clear.  This was a direct pull from our internal, and needs a lot of cleanup."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0005-Adding-Mctp-Over-Spi-Driver.patch",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "Given this looks like it interacts with a particular spi peripheral (\"SBP?\"), I'd suggest adjusting the naming to reflect that.\n\nWe would want to reserve `CONFIG_MCTP_TRANSPORT_SPI` / `mctp-spi` for a DMTF-defined transport type."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0005-Adding-Mctp-Over-Spi-Driver.patch",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "You're not going to be able to submit this upstream with an Apache-2.0 license.  Hopefully this is known by your team.\n\n```\n$ cat LICENSES/dual/Apache-2.0\nValid-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\nSPDX-URL: https://spdx.org/licenses/Apache-2.0.html\nUsage-Guide:\n  Do NOT use. The Apache-2.0 is not GPL2 compatible. It may only be used\n  for dual-licensed files where the other license is GPL2 compatible.\n  If you end up using this it MUST be used together with a GPL2 compatible\n  license using \"OR\".\n  To use the Apache License version 2.0 put the following SPDX tag/value\n  pair into a comment according to the placement guidelines in the\n  licensing rules documentation:\n    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n```\n\nEvery file in the kernel with Apache-2.0 SPDX is either \"Apache-2.0 OR MIT\" or \"GPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0005-Adding-Mctp-Over-Spi-Driver.patch",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ACK.  Yeah, this license is wrong, should've been GPL.  Will change in next push."
                }
            ],
